From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:42:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/PlatformBootManagerLib: Keep a tried slot
 before updates

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0046, as it is]

The payload tells coreboot that the vboot slot it booted works once the
console is up (PlatformMarkFirmwareGood ()), so that vboot keeps a slot
that it tries after an update. A boot with update capsules resets after
applying them, before that: if vboot was trying the slot that runs, the
boot used one of its tries. An update that fails then, or that is
refused before it writes anything, can use up the tries of a slot that
works, and vboot goes back to the other one.

Tell coreboot that the slot works before the updates as well, once the
console is up and the power is enough: the slot booted as far as it does
when a normal boot marks it. This comes before an update writes
RW_NVRAM, so the request to try the other slot follows it.

TEST=tools/qemu-update.py of ouroBIOS: a capsule refused while vboot
tries the slot that runs, with a try left, keeps that slot ("firmware
slot marked good before the updates: Success", the result "success" in
RW_NVRAM, no try of the other slot); the capsules that write the other
slot still have vboot try it.
---
 .../Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c
index 21fb4f3..f82b146 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c
@@ -619,6 +619,18 @@ PlatformProcessCapsules (
       CapsuleMessage (UpdateScreenToneWarning, L"Battery too low, firmware update postponed");
       gBS->Stall (CAPSULE_MESSAGE_DELAY);
     } else {
+      //
+      // This slot booted as far as the console: if vboot is trying it,
+      // keep it now, before an update asks vboot to try the other slot.
+      // The reset after the updates comes before PlatformMarkFirmwareGood ():
+      // without this, an update that fails, or that is refused before it
+      // writes anything, uses up a try of a slot that works.
+      //
+      Status = SmmStoreLibVbootSlotGood ();
+      if (Status != EFI_UNSUPPORTED) {
+        DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "Capsules: firmware slot marked good before the updates: %r\n", Status));
+      }
+
       if (InMemory) {
         Applied = TRUE;
         Status  = ProcessCapsules ();
-- 
